# Runtime data / scan output. Anchored to the repo root: an unanchored `data/` also
# matched `core/data/`, which silently kept the scope engine's bundled CDN/cloud
# ranges out of git. Local builds worked because Docker copies the working tree; a
# release built from a clean checkout would have shipped without it and crashed on
# startup. See tests/unit/test_wiring.py::test_the_bundled_scope_feed_is_committed.
/data/
*.log
scope_feeds_cache/
for-claude-referece/

# -- licensing / control plane secrets (NEVER commit) --
*.pem
*.vlic
license-keys/
docker/cp-secrets/
docker/cp.env
cp-data/
age-identity*.txt

# Raw scan logs kept locally as a working reference. Never commit these: a real scan
# log is a full external attack-surface map of whatever was scanned (hostnames, live
# URLs, technologies), and this repo is public. It was committed once and had to be
# removed from history.
logs-for-claue.txt
*-logs.txt
